      "obligation": "refuter:30:1",
      "id": "thm-hll-flux-is-consistent-and-conservative",
      "location": "Title and Statement; Proof 1.1",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The dependency `def-rankine-hugoniot-and-lax-shocks` defines a Rankine–Hugoniot jump by `f(u_R)-f(u_L)=s(u_R-u_L)`. For Burgers flux `f(u)=u^2/2` on `G=R`, states `u_L=0,u_R=1`, and enclosing speeds `S_L=-1,S_R=2`, the stated formula gives `u_*=1/2`. The physical left jump would require `f(1/2)-f(0)=-1/2`, but its left side is `1/8`. Proof 1.1 instead defines an auxiliary `f_*=-1/2` and verifies balance for that value; it does not establish `f_*=f(u_*)`. Thus the HLL middle flux formula follows from the assigned model flux, but the stated physical Rankine–Hugoniot claim does not.",
